# Runtime data.
#
# These are ANCHORED with a leading slash so they match only at the repo
# root. Unanchored, "config/" matches internal/config/ at any depth — which
# it did, silently excluding a whole package from the commit that
# introduced it and breaking the build on CI while it compiled fine
# locally. git status does not show what it is ignoring.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3
/config/
/data/
/logs/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
CLAUDE.md
/.claude
/team
